=== CORRECTION (kps-S4, approach-from-above test) ===
The "0 failures for |L|=3,4" above used Vmax>=60; with SMALL Vmax the via-max criterion DOES fail:
 |L|=3 min via-max margin = 147/208 ~ 0.707 at {1,2,3,6,8,9,10,11,12,13,14,15,21} (Vmax=21)
 |L|=4 min via-max margin = 242/273 ~ 0.886 at {1,3,4,8,9,10,11,12,13,14,18,21,22} (Vmax=22)
So the criterion-failures for |L| in {3,4} live at SMALL Vmax (large speeds barely >13). CORRECTED
split: |L| in {3,4} closes EXACTLY like the PROVED k=2 slice — pigeonhole gives the limit margin
>= 7/c - 1 (c=|L|-1 <=3: c=2 ->5/2, c=3 ->4/3, both >1) for the large-Vmax regime, and a FINITE
CORE (bounded Vmax) below the threshold. Only |L|>=5 (cluster' >=4 pts, no pigeonhole) is the
genuine rho* hard case (mac-mini THM-527). LIMIT margin lower bound: w_theta >= 1/c - 1/7 (since
maxgap >= 1/c), so margin = 7*w_theta >= 7/c - 1.
